6Stabilizing a head or spinal injury
The aim of first aid for spinal injuries is to prevent further injury, 
by preventing movement of the injured area. When moving 
the casualty is necessary, support them in a way that minimizes 
movement of the head and spine.
1. As soon as you suspect a head or spinal injury, tell the 
casualty not to move. Steady and support the casualty’s 
head and neck as soon as you can—show a bystander how 
to do this: 
• Keep elbows on the ground to keep arms steady.
• Firmly hold the head with fingers along the line of the 
jaw. 
2. Show a second bystander how to steady and support the 
feet. The head and feet should be continuously supported 
until either the casualty is fully immobilized or medical help 
takes over. 
